# sync-skills ignore list (example)
#
# Copy this file to `sync-skills.ignore` (same directory) and add the names of
# installed skills you DON'T want /sync-skills to flag as "not present in
# devkit/skills". Useful for skills you installed separately and don't want
# devkit to manage.
#
# `sync-skills.ignore` is gitignored — your entries stay local and never reach
# this public repo. Only this .example file is committed.
#
# Format: one entry per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored; a `#` after an
# entry starts a trailing comment (stripped).
#   <name>        ignore a skill by name in every environment
#   <env>/<name>  ignore only in that environment (env = claude | codex | cursor)
#
# Examples:
# notebooklm
# claude/some-installed-skill   # only ignored in Claude Code
